  "description": "LILXEL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C62 H60 Ho6 N46 O2 Se2,8(C5 H5 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 1 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 1 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 2 O neighbors; Ho1A (Ho) has 1 O neighbors; Ho2A (Ho) has 1 O neighbors; Ho3A (Ho) has 2 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.579-3.753 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.84-112.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (py)10Ho6O2(N3)12(SePh)2·8(py).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
